<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine pension funds yield 22.15 percent.</title>
<headline>Argentine pension funds yield 22.15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's private pension funds averaged a return of 22.15 percent on their investments in the year to March, the Superintendency of Pension and Retirement Funds, the body that monitors the funds, said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In the year to February, the funds, known by their Spanish acronym AFJPs, achieved an average return of 20.25 percent.</p>
<p>The maximum return attained in the year to March was 28.79 percent, while the lowest was 15.50 percent, the Superintendency said.</p>
<p>The average annual return since the private pension funds were first established in the middle of 1994 was 18.70 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Walter Bianchi, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0651))</p>
</text>
